            <ArticleTitle>Chronic pancreatitis: an update for home care and hospice clinicians.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>562-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/NHH.0b013e31822eb6e2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic pancreatitis is a relentlessly painful condition associated most commonly with alcoholism. Patients suffer wasting and depression as a result of chronic pain. It is important for home care clinicians to recognize the signs of pancreatitis and understand the current evidence-based treatment strategies to control the symptoms. Although alcoholism and depression are frequent comorbidities of pancreatitis, a full discussion of alcoholism and depression is outside the scope of this article.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
